<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>出版物 |皮尤研究中心</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/publications/</link><description>塑造您世界的数字、事实和趋势</description><lastBuildDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 03:20:37 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>美国人如何参与在线新闻？</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/10/07/how-do-americans-engage-with-news-online/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/10/SR_26.10.07_online-engagement_topic.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;大多数美国人在网上私下谈论新闻，但只有大约四分之一的人公开发布新闻。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 03:20:37 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/10/07/how-do-americans-engage-with-news-online/</guid></item><item><title>健康和保健影响者发布的内容是什么？</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/data-labs/2026/10/07/what-do-health-and-wellness-influencers-post-about/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/10/pl_2026.10.07_health-influencers-featured-image.jpg?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;社交媒体上超过一半的健康内容关注健康生活，约三分之一讨论医疗话题。 38% 的帖子有产品或服务促销。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 03:20:37 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/data-labs/2026/10/07/what-do-health-and-wellness-influencers-post-about/</guid></item><item><title>为什么美国人认为自己是共和党人和民主党人——以及为什么他们不认为自己是共和党人和民主党人</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/10/02/why-americans-identify-as-republicans-and-democrats-and-why-they-dont/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/10/SR_26.10.02_partisanship-reasons_crop.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;许多人不认为自己是共和党人或民主党人。相反，他们是独立人士或其他人——尽管他们经常“倾向于”主要政党。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 02:40:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/10/02/why-americans-identify-as-republicans-and-democrats-and-why-they-dont/</guid></item><item><title>澳大利亚人如何看待儿童社交媒体限制？</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/10/01/what-do-australians-think-about-social-media-restrictions-for-kids/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/09/SR_26.10.01_australia-social-media_featured.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;大约十分之八的澳大利亚成年人支持限制儿童使用社交媒体。其中51%的人强烈支持。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 17:38:06 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/10/01/what-do-australians-think-about-social-media-restrictions-for-kids/</guid></item><item><title>在全球范围内，越来越多的人认为社交媒体正在损害民主</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2026/10/01/across-the-globe-people-increasingly-say-social-media-is-harming-democracy/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/09/PG_26.09.00_SocialMediaDem_featured@2x.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;大多数人认为社交媒体会导致操纵和分裂，但他们也表示社交媒体可以为人们提供信息并让他们在政治中拥有发言权。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 17:38:06 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2026/10/01/across-the-globe-people-increasingly-say-social-media-is-harming-democracy/</guid></item></channel></rss>